{:id "0052-lab-dress"
 :title "Lab dress: what a mark leaves behind (versal, rubric, gilt, strong, whisper), and gold that catches the pointer"
 :lupa/deps #{"0050-lab-reading"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'Dress' and 'Illumination, now', and
        hypothesis H7 in docs/product/lab-notebook.md. Gestures return to
        rest; dress is what stays, the way bold does. On the paper page
        (reveal level 1) a dressed draft should look like a page from a
        manuscript: a raised initial, a red-letter phrase, a word in gold,
        a whispered aside. And the gold is alive without moving: it
        brightens under the pointer, as gold leaf caught a candle."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/dress_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/reading_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs"
         "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/debug_test.cljc"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "Schema (the foreman's; do not edit): :ha/dress, :ha/ink, the
          optional keys of :ha/glyph-pose.
          First, a fix to order 0050 that its builder reported and the
          foreman's design caused: lab.reading/natural-ms takes a style
          point and uses (style/from-point point)'s tempo, but lab.pose
          plays a named style at (style/params style), so an Elegant
          gesture (tempo 1.5, not 1.36) runs about 10% longer than the
          reading grants and its cue is withdrawn during its tail. Make
          the reading use the tempo actually in force: natural-ms and plan
          take the motion parameters that lab.pose will play with (params
          for a named style, from-point for a point) alongside the point
          that chooses gestures and dress; lab.main passes both. Test: for
          each named style, every cue of a reading of the acceptance
          sentence ends (by lab.pose's own timing) no later than the
          reading is over?, and no cue is withdrawn while a letter is
          still off rest.
          halfahead.lab.dress (.cljc, pure):
          looks -> a public map, what each dress does to a letter at rest:
            :versal  {:size 1.8}                      ; a raised initial
            :rubric  {:ink :signal}
            :gilt    {:ink :gold :glint true}
            :strong  {:weight 0.55}
            :whisper {:size 0.85 :ink :muted :weight -0.2}
          (placed dress glyphs) -> [{:as kw :glyph-ids [..]}], each dress's
            span as glyph ids (a glyph's offset is the sum of the UTF-16
            lengths of the glyphs before it, as lab.reading does); a dress
            whose span holds no glyph is left out.
          (seen prev placed t) -> {[as first-glyph-id] since-ms}: when each
            placed dress was first seen, keeping earlier times from prev
            and dropping dress that is gone (the shell keeps this between
            frames; it is the only memory dress needs).
          (sizes placed glyphs) -> {glyph-id size} for glyphs whose dress
            changes their size (a glyph in two such dress takes the
            larger change from 1).
          (at-rest pose look w light) -> pose with the look applied at
            weight w (0 to 1): :ink the look's ink with :tint w; :weight
            w x the look's; and for :glint, :glow raised by the light: 0.12
            w with no light, else w x (0.12 + 0.5 e^(-d^2 / (2 x 1.2^2))),
            d the distance in em from the light to the letter (x, y).
          lab.pose: frame's opts gain :dress {:placed [...] :seen {...}
            :light {:x :y} or nil}. From reveal level 1 up: layout uses
            each glyph's size (its advance multiplied, so nothing overlaps
            and lines wrap as they should); a sized glyph's pose is
            scaled by its size and kept on the baseline at its left edge
            (shift x by half (size - 1) x advance and y by 0.35 (size - 1),
            as a :card does); each dressed live pose gets its look at
            weight w = smoothstep((t - since) / 500), so dress eases in
            over half a second; size eases the same way (1 toward size).
            With reduced motion w is 1 at once. At level 0, and with no
            :dress, frames are exactly as before. The caret follows the
            sized layout. All existing invariants hold with dress: the
            live poses spell the draft; cues and shots perform on top of
            the dressed rest; sideways motion stays within half an em of
            the dressed place.
          lab.render: only if needed to draw a sized or tinted glyph
            correctly; no new draw call.
          lab.main: after every edit, and when the style changes, the
            draft's dress is (score/from-text text point)'s :dress for the
            style point in force, placed on the glyphs; seen is updated
            each frame; the pointer's position over the stage, projected
            onto the text plane in em (render has the camera), is the
            :light, nil when the pointer is away or the device has none.
            window.__lab.dress() -> the placed dress as plain data. The
            debug overlay lists it ('dress: gilt \"the one thing\" ·
            whisper \"trust me\"').
          Tests: placed and sizes for each dress, with emoji before the
          span; seen keeps, adds and drops; at-rest for each look at w 0,
          0.5 and 1, and the glint against distance; pose: a versal's
          neighbours do not overlap it and the line's width grows by 0.8 of
          its advance; a whisper narrows its span; dress eases in and is
          instant with reduced motion; level 0 ignores dress; and every
          existing pose test passes unchanged. Property: for generated
          drafts and dress, the frame is valid, live poses spell the
          draft, and no two neighbouring letters on a line overlap at rest.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'dress', by data and stills:
          (a) /lab/?debug&reveal=1 (paper), Elegant picked: type 'This is
          *the one thing* that matters (trust me).', wait 1 s: the glyphs
          of 'the one thing' carry ink gold and tint 1, those of 'trust
          me' are smaller than 1 and muted; the most common inked colour
          inside the gold word's box matches lab.ink's gold for paper;
          screenshot out/lab/dress-paper.png. (b) move the mouse over the
          gold word: its letters' :glow in lastFrame rises above 0.4; move
          it away: back to about 0.12. (c) Caffeinated picked, a sentence
          of 14 words: the first letter's scale is about 1.8 and the
          second letter starts at or beyond the first's scaled right edge.
          (d) the same on the dark stage (?reveal=3): screenshot
          out/lab/dress-dark.png. (e) Plain picked: no dress at all.
          docs/LAB.md: a section 'Dress' (the five, when the rules give
          them, the glint, that dress is presentation and never text)."
 :acceptance
 ["dress and pose tests as in the design, on both hosts"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the dress step and every existing step; `bb
   test` stays green; the two dress screenshots for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["No dropped (multi-line) initials; no borders, pictures or marginal
   glosses (later releases); no time-based shimmer: the glint follows the
   pointer only"
  "No change to marks, score, gestures, synth, pace, the board, the
   director, reveal levels or the stage; do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "docs/product/lab-notebook.md"
           "src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/score.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/marks.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/ink.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/render.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
